{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2131201979/12/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/12`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2131201979/12/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：识别网格中的小矩形\"种子图案\"和 grey 边界围成的封闭区域，通过区域内标记像素的颜色配对种子图案，再将种子图案周期性平铺填充到对应区域内部。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干个小的矩形种子图案（如 2x2 或 3x3），每个种子图案由两种颜色组成（例如 blue 和 yellow 的棋盘格，或 red 和 green 的条纹），不同种子图案使用不同的颜色组合。\n  - 在网格中另有若干个较大的不规则封闭区域，每个区域的边界由 grey 像素勾画（grey 像素形成封闭的环形边界）。每个封闭区域内部为 black。\n  - 每个封闭区域内恰好有一个单像素标记，该标记的颜色与某个种子图案中使用的某一种颜色匹配——以此作为配对线索。每种颜色只会出现在一个种子图案中，保证唯一配对。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个封闭区域，找到其内部的单像素标记颜色。\n  - 在所有种子图案中，找到包含该标记颜色的那个种子图案。\n  - 以种子图案为单元，从封闭区域外接矩形的左上角开始对齐，对整个封闭区域进行周期性平铺——即区域内部每个像素的位置，根据该像素相对于外接矩形左上角的坐标对种子图案的宽高取余，取种子图案对应位置的颜色。\n  - 区域的 grey 边界保持不变。\n  - 种子图案本身在输出中被清除为 black（仅作为参考信息使用）。\n  - 标记像素被平铺图案覆盖。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现标记颜色与种子图案之间的配对关系（颜色归属），再理解种子图案是一个周期平铺单元而非简单的颜色填充。两层推理缺一不可：配对是第一层，平铺机制是第二层。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/88e364bc, train/84551f4c, train/5adee1b2, train/db7260a4, eval/dbff022c, train/57edb29d, train/3cd86f4f, train/aa62e3f4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2990\nmechanism=0.3333\nlexical=0.0187\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"84551f4c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2338\nmechanism=0.2506\nlexical=0.0167\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:marker, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/84551f4c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/84551f4c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate each blue-started chain of bottom-aligned vertical bars into horizontal bars resting on the same baseline.\nInput structure\n- The grid has a background and bottom-aligned, one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Blue bars are markers; red bars are body bars that may be chained after a marker.\nRule\n- Starting at each blue bar, repeatedly include the next red bar whose column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height.\n- Clear every included vertical bar, then redraw each included bar horizontally to the right from its original bottom cell, with length equal to its vertical height.\n- Red bars that are not reached from a blue marker remain unchanged.\nKey insight\n- A vertical bar's height is also the width it occupies after rotation, so the chain follows immediate horizontal contact after each rotated bar.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars on the background; blue bars start chains and red bars may follow\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each blue-started chain, rotate each reached vertical bar clockwise onto the shared baseline; the next red bar is reached when its column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5adee1b2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2504\nmechanism=0.3053\nlexical=0.0143\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5adee1b2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nUse the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color.\n- One or more two-row markers sit on the left edge; each marker is a 2x2 block whose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.\n- Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input pixels unchanged.\n- For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.\n- Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.\n\nKey insight:\n- The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected monochrome objects on the background plus left-edge two-column color legend markers\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each object whose color appears in the legend, fill background pixels in its one-cell padded bbox with the paired legend color; preserve the object and any enclosed background holes\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"left-edge two-column legend maps object color to bbox-fill color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db7260a4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2636\nmechanism=0.3247\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, output:same_size, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db7260a4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/db7260a4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,\n  and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.\n- A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous\n  bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.\n\nRule\n- Remove the top marker from its original cell.\n- If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its\n  horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.\n- If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row\n  with the marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop\n  column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"singleton top-row marker pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop down the marker column; a closed U-shaped wall container catches the drop when the marker column lies within its horizontal footprint, otherwise the path reaches the bottom edge\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed U-shaped container interior, or the bottom row if no closed container catches the drop\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill the caught container's background interior with the marker color; if uncaught, fill the whole bottom row\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the original marker pixel and keep all wall pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2601\nmechanism=0.2909\nlexical=0.0114\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, operation:flood_fill, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
